**Read:** [Tratamento de Minérios — CETEM, sixth edition](../sources/Tratamento-de-Minerios-CETEM.lingua#r_04ZQFADZ3NC3T6QDPQ565W1ERA), the complete electrical/electrostatic separation chapter; [Tratamento de Minérios: Práticas Laboratoriais — Sampaio, França, and Braga](../sources/CETEM-Praticas-Laboratoriais.lingua#r_44AAWXB1D7MBR9B0V3TYB8GF9B), the full relevant preparation/conditioning/separation methods; [Usinas de Beneficiamento de Minérios do Brasil — CETEM](../sources/CETEM-Usinas-de-Beneficiamento.lingua#r_62ZD994C9YYXB1YDVFQST5B27J), a complete applicable case and primary method reference.

Electrical/electrostatic separation connects charging or conductivity behavior with particle size, shape, association, surface state, contact history, fields, geometry, motion, and environmental conditions. A mineral's bulk electrical classification does not fully determine every prepared particle's trajectory.

Moisture, coatings, impurities, temperature, contamination, and handling can alter surface/conductivity response. A laboratory result requires its preparation and conditioning account before transfer to another feed or scale. Fine intergrowth and mixed/aggregated particles can limit selectivity.

Separate apparatus/settings, measured material properties, a force/trajectory model, and observed stream partition. Product quality, recovery, throughput, environmental controls, maintenance, and energy should share a clear basis. Stable operation with representative feed needs more evidence than one favorable batch result.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete electrical-separation case with preparation, method, environmental conditions, particle population, sampling, and uncertainty. Independently check a stream/constituent balance and a stated model relation within its domain. Compare an alternative involving surface state or association and identify the experiment needed to distinguish it.

Read full theory and laboratory methods with the equipment's actual professional guidance. The next surface-chemistry/flotation sequence develops another form of selectivity whose response also depends on both mineral identity and changing interfaces.

**Continue:** [Test sensor-based sorting against measured particles and the complete feed account](Sensor-based-sorting-observability-and-rejection.lingua#r_1C2JP9GAXHD912MVT0WS8Q071G).

